WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.634
-Our next guest is the
co-host of the "U Up?" podcast

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.167
available at Apple Podcasts.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.167
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:11.133
please welcome the very funny
Jared Freid!

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.934
-How we doing, everybody?!
We good?!

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:25.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.701
I do a lot of shows.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.100
I've performed for the troops,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.100
and those shows
are always the best.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
The best.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.367
I also perform at colleges.
Those shows are always weird.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.400
I was at a college once.
I came onstage.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.200
My first words out of
my mouth -- I said,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.300
"I love doing shows
for college kids."

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.601
This guy stands up in the corner
and he goes, "We're not kids!

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.601
We're adults!"

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:58.033
I look at him.
I go, "One question.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.801
Who bought your underwear?"

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:10.400
I'll never forget it.
He goes, "Go on with the show."

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.133
I get that.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.267
I thought I was
an adult in college.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.767
I definitely was not.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:21.467
I used to wear one polo shirt
with another polo shirt over it.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.200
Yeah. And then pop up
both of the collars.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.567
That's not how an adult dresses.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:34.534
There's no adult walking around
like an aggressive tulip.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.300
My girlfriend --
she would wear two polos, too.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.734
Two people, four polos.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.067
When we hooked up,
it looked like

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.234
a Brooks Brothers fitting room.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.167
You're not an adult in college.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.567
One semester, I lived with three
of my friends in one room.

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:57.567
We called it "Bunkzilla."

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:01.033
No man lives in a Bunkzilla.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.701
If a man lives guys three other
men, that's not a home.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.334
That's a shelter.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:10.968
And no woman here would go home
to Bunkzilla tonight.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.267
That's the difference in
college -- they would.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.734
One night,
we all brought women home.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.267
That's right --
one room, four beds,

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.601
eight people...

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.834
16 polos.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.000
I don't know.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.968
I think people don't like
college students

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.834
because they speak confidently
on things we know

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.133
they can't be
confident about yet.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.567
Like, the two stories are
always written

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.868
that they're
outraged or they're shamed.

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.901
I didn't know
outrage in college.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.634
I learned about outrage
the first time

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:53.300
I saw the taxes
that come out of a paycheck.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.334
Right? That weird moment
where you're like,

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.734
"I don't even use roads."

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:05.567
I learned shame the first time
I laughed at a boss's joke.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.901
You wouldn't do that
in front of your child.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.200
You'd be like,
"Turn around, Timmy.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.801
Daddy's got to pay rent.
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:19.000
You're right.
Mondays are weird."

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.734
I don't even know
what an adult is any more.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:23.767
I'm 36.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:24.968
I'm doing stuff I thought
I would have

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.100
grown up out of years ago.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.400
Every time I fly somewhere,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.400
I text my parents, "Landed."

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.133
You ever read
that text back to yourself?

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.467
You don't sound like a man.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:42.467
"Landed."

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:43.834
You sound like a spoiled prince.

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:48.400
"Mommy, put my jammies
in the dryer.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.701
I prefer them warm
with my milk and cookies.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:55.300
Tell papa I'll be taking
story time in my quarters.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.133
The Prince of Needham
has landed!"

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.634
I love going home
for the holidays.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.501
I like seeing my family.

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:12.801
I like seeing where all
my insecurities came from.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.601
Right? If your family
has a problem,

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.334
you probably have
a very similar problem.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:18.000
My family --
the whole family is insecure.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.634
Food, body, weight.
That's our whole family.

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:23.067
I walked in the house one day.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.501
My mom looks at me.
She goes, "You look so skinny."

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:26.801
My dad's across the room.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:30.734
He yells out -- He goes,
"He's wearing all black!"

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.567
I was like, "Is my inner
monologue playing on the Alexa?"

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.200
I talk about
my weight onstage a lot.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.567
Some people
get very uncomfortable.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.067
I had a woman --
She stood up once.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:47.701
She goes, "You're not fat."

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:49.000
That's the worst thing
you could ever yell

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.400
at someone who's not skinny.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.367
Because then the show
becomes a town-hall meeting

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.667
on whether I'm fat or not.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:58.734
Someone stood up.

00:04:58.734 --> 00:05:02.400
They're like,
"He's jolly, though."

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.300
Another person was like,
"Can men be curvy?"

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.133
Someone in the middle was like,
"There's lead in the water."

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:12.033
I was like, "You're at
the wrong meeting, bro."

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:20.501
I just want to get
in shape enough

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:23.901
to take a vacation to
Tulum, Mexico.

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:25.701
If you know Tulum,
that's where all the

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.534
celebrities and influencers go.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:30.601
I've never seen someone
there with a bad body.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:34.234
I think they weigh you
at the Mexican border.

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:35.400
Like, I think
I would get to Mexico.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.767
They'd be like, "Hola.
Step on the scale."

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:40.067
I'd step on. They'd look down.

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:43.267
They'd be like,
"Well, have fun in Cancún."

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:45.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.033
I'm Jared Freid.
Thank you guys very much.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:50.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:54.067
-16 polos.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.467
-The best.
-Thank you.

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:58.834
-Jared Freid!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.834 --> 00:06:02.467
The "U Up?" podcast
is available on Apple Podcasts.

